{
  "actors": [
    {
      "id": "producer",
      "label": "Producer",
      "role": "producer",
      "x": 18,
      "y": 86
    },
    {
      "id": "broker",
      "label": "Broker log",
      "role": "broker",
      "x": 18,
      "y": 62
    },
    {
      "id": "consumer",
      "label": "Consumer",
      "role": "consumer",
      "x": 50,
      "y": 62
    },
    {
      "id": "ledger",
      "label": "Ledger DB",
      "role": "store",
      "x": 50,
      "y": 38
    },
    {
      "id": "card",
      "label": "Card API",
      "role": "external",
      "x": 50,
      "y": 86
    }
  ],
  "meters": [
    {"id": "del", "label": "Times pay-7 delivered to the consumer", "max": 2},
    {"id": "rows", "label": "Ledger rows for pay-7", "max": 2, "warnAt": 2},
    {"id": "card", "label": "Charged to the card ($)", "max": 100, "warnAt": 51}
  ],
  "frames": [
    {
      "narration": "The producer appends 'charge $50 for order 7' (pay-7) to the log at offset 41. The consumer's job: charge the card and write one ledger row, exactly once.",
      "meters": {"del": 1, "rows": 0, "card": 0},
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "producer",
          "to": "broker",
          "label": "pay-7 $50"
        },
        {
          "from": "broker",
          "to": "consumer",
          "label": "offset 41"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "broker": "offset 41 stored",
        "ledger": "empty",
        "card": "$0"
      }
    },
    {
      "narration": "At-most-once: the offset is committed first (ack-before). The consumer crashes before charging. The broker already moved on to 42 and never redelivers, so pay-7 is lost.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "consumer",
          "to": "broker",
          "label": "ack 41"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "broker": "committed 42",
        "consumer": "crashed",
        "ledger": "empty",
        "card": "$0"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "consumer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "At-least-once: process first, ack after. This time the consumer charges the card and writes the ledger row, then crashes before the ack reaches the broker.",
      "meters": {"rows": 1, "card": 50},
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "consumer",
          "to": "card",
          "label": "charge $50"
        },
        {
          "from": "consumer",
          "to": "ledger",
          "label": "insert pay-7"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "broker": "committed 41 (no ack)",
        "consumer": "crashed",
        "ledger": "pay-7 $50",
        "card": "$50"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "consumer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "The ack timeout expires and the broker redelivers offset 41. The consumer cannot know it already ran, so it charges again: the customer now has $100 charged and two ledger rows.",
      "meters": {"del": 2, "rows": 2, "card": 100},
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "broker",
          "to": "consumer",
          "label": "redeliver 41"
        },
        {
          "from": "consumer",
          "to": "card",
          "label": "charge $50"
        },
        {
          "from": "consumer",
          "to": "ledger",
          "label": "insert pay-7"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "consumer": "restarted",
        "ledger": "pay-7 x2 = $100",
        "card": "$100"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "ledger",
        "card"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "Fix 1, idempotent consumer: insert the business id pay-7 into a dedupe table (unique key) in the same transaction as the ledger row. On redelivery the insert is rejected, the consumer skips the work and acks.",
      "meters": {"rows": 1},
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "broker",
          "to": "consumer",
          "label": "redeliver 41"
        },
        {
          "from": "consumer",
          "to": "ledger",
          "label": "insert pay-7?"
        },
        {
          "from": "ledger",
          "to": "consumer",
          "label": "already seen"
        },
        {
          "from": "consumer",
          "to": "broker",
          "label": "ack 41"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "broker": "committed 42",
        "ledger": "pay-7 $50 once",
        "consumer": "skipped"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "ledger"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "The guarantee ends at the database. The card charge is outside the transaction: a crash between the card call and the commit would repeat it. So the charge carries Idempotency-Key: pay-7 and the provider returns the first result.",
      "meters": {"card": 50},
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "consumer",
          "to": "card",
          "label": "key pay-7"
        },
        {
          "from": "card",
          "to": "consumer",
          "label": "same charge"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "card": "$50 once",
        "consumer": "retry is safe"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "card"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "Fix 2, transactional consumer: the ledger row and the new offset 42 commit in one transaction. A crash leaves both or neither, so there is no half-state to redeliver from. A duplicate produced upstream still needs a producer id or a business-id check.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "consumer",
          "to": "ledger",
          "label": "row + offset 42"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "ledger": "pay-7 $50, offset 42",
        "broker": "no ack needed"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "ledger"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "Result: ledger $50 once, card $50 once, however the crashes fell. The network still delivered pay-7 twice; the system made the second delivery harmless. That is effectively-once.",
      "states": {
        "ledger": "pay-7 $50 once",
        "card": "$50 once",
        "consumer": "idempotent"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "ledger",
        "card"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
